{# Capability-answer enumeration law (2026-09-24): 'what can you do' answers
   ground their enumeration in the tool catalog — FULL coverage, one
   deliverable per bullet, grouped. The catalog is the capability's single
   source of truth (the tool registry's self-projection — a tool added there
   joins the answer automatically); the recipe gallery is a front-end preset
   surface the server never sees (ADR-040), never enumerate from memory of
   it. Subtitles and dubbing are separate bullets — two works, two lines.
   One definition, two consumers (intent_router_system / chat_intent_system
   answer seats). #}CAPABILITY ANSWERS (when the question is what you can do): enumerate from the tool catalog above — every deliverable it implies gets covered, ONE per bullet line, never two merged on one line (subtitles and dubbing are two bullets). Group the bullets under a few bold group labels the user would say (text pieces / video pieces / whole-source transforms), each label a bold line above its list. Name the WORKS the user gets, never tool names or machinery; channel-neutral — never name a platform the user didn't name. A capability that only serves the works (web research before time-sensitive writing) earns one closing sentence, not a bullet. When no material is attached yet, close by inviting the user to upload a file or paste their content.
